msgstr "Interface tweaks"

msgid "General"
msgstr "General"

msgid "Enabled"
msgstr "Enabled"

msgid "Research and crafting queues"
msgstr "Research and crafting queues"

msgid "Row height, px"
msgstr "Row height, px"

msgid "0 - the game's height."
msgstr "0 - the game's height."

msgid "Bar inset, px"
msgstr "Bar inset, px"

msgid "0 - the bar is left to the game."
msgstr "0 - the bar is left to the game."

msgid "Squads tab"
msgstr "Squads tab"

msgid "Rows of portraits"
msgstr "Rows of portraits"

msgid "Grow with the largest squad"
msgstr "Grow with the largest squad"

msgid "Next level bar"
msgstr "Next level bar"

msgid "Frame padding, px"
msgstr "Frame padding, px"

msgid "Lower by, px"
msgstr "Lower by, px"

msgid "Raise the top edge by, px"
msgstr "Raise the top edge by, px"

msgid "Description panels"
msgstr "Description panels"

msgid "Scroll bar"
msgstr "Scroll bar"

msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr "Diagnostics"

msgid "Detailed log"
msgstr "Detailed log"

msgid "Details in RE_Kenshi_log.txt."
msgstr "Details in RE_Kenshi_log.txt."

msgid "Interface fixes that layouts cannot do: queues, bars, squad cells, scrolling descriptions."
msgstr "Interface fixes that layouts cannot do: queues, bars, squad cells, scrolling descriptions."

msgid "Interface fixes that layouts cannot do. Each one can be turned off below."
msgstr "Interface fixes that layouts cannot do. Each one can be turned off below."

msgid "Row height in the research and crafting queues. The game gives about 16 and Russian text does not fit. 0 - the game's height."
msgstr "Row height in the research and crafting queues. The game gives about 16 and Russian text does not fit. 0 - the game's height."

msgid "Gap between the progress fill and the row frame. The plugin draws its own fill across the whole frame. 0 - the bar is left to the game."
msgstr "Gap between the progress fill and the row frame. The plugin draws its own fill across the whole frame. 0 - the bar is left to the game."

msgid "How many rows of portraits fit in a squad cell on the Squads tab without cutting. 0 - the game's height."
msgstr "How many rows of portraits fit in a squad cell on the Squads tab without cutting. 0 - the game's height."

msgid "When the largest squad needs more rows, all cells grow - the list has one height for all. Off - extra fighters go under the scroll."
msgstr "When the largest squad needs more rows, all cells grow - the list has one height for all. Off - extra fighters go under the scroll."

msgid "How much taller the frame of the Next level bar in the skill description is, at the top and the bottom. 0 - the bar is left to the game."
msgstr "How much taller the frame of the Next level bar in the skill description is, at the top and the bottom. 0 - the bar is left to the game."

msgid "Moves the bar with its frame down without moving the text, so the text looks centred. Lines below move by the same amount."
msgstr "Moves the bar with its frame down without moving the text, so the text looks centred. Lines below move by the same amount."

msgid "Raises only the top edge of the bar frame. The bottom edge and the text stay where they are."
msgstr "Raises only the top edge of the bar frame. The bottom edge and the text stay where they are."

msgid "A scroll bar in the description panels of research and items, so long text is not cut off."
msgstr "A scroll bar in the description panels of research and items, so long text is not cut off."

msgid "Lists every description panel created and its flags in RE_Kenshi_log.txt - useful if the scroll bar did not appear."
msgstr "Lists every description panel created and its flags in RE_Kenshi_log.txt - useful if the scroll bar did not appear."

msgid "Hints"
msgstr "Hints"

msgid "Faction relation by the name"
msgstr "Faction relation by the name"

msgid "After the faction name of the selected character - that faction's relation to you, like in the factions window: green above zero, red from -10 down."
msgstr "After the faction name of the selected character - that faction's relation to you, like in the factions window: green above zero, red from -10 down."



msgid "Item icon in the crafting list"
msgstr "Item icon in the crafting list"

msgid "On the Crafting tab, the icon of the item appears next to the mouse over a line of the Items list."
msgstr "On the Crafting tab, the icon of the item appears next to the mouse over a line of the Items list."

msgid "Draw icons of all items"
msgstr "Draw icons of all items"

msgid "The game draws an item icon only when the item first gets into an inventory. This draws them now for every item without one, a few per frame, in a loaded game. The pictures stay in data/icons."
msgstr "The game draws an item icon only when the item first gets into an inventory. This draws them now for every item without one, a few per frame, in a loaded game. The pictures stay in data/icons."

msgid "Load a game first - icons are drawn in the game world."
msgstr "Load a game first - icons are drawn in the game world."

msgid "Drawing item icons: %u / %u"
msgstr "Drawing item icons: %u / %u"

msgid "Item icons done: %u drawn, %u could not be drawn"
msgstr "Item icons done: %u drawn, %u could not be drawn"

msgid "Icon key"
msgstr "Icon key"

msgid "The icon shows while this key is held. NONE (Backspace when assigning) - on hover alone."
msgstr "The icon shows while this key is held. NONE (Backspace when assigning) - on hover alone."

msgid "Faction relation key"
msgstr "Faction relation key"

msgid "The relation shows while this key is held. NONE (Backspace when assigning) - always."
msgstr "The relation shows while this key is held. NONE (Backspace when assigning) - always."

msgid "Trader window"
msgstr "Trader window"

msgid "Money at the centre"
msgstr "Money at the centre"

msgid "The trader's money at the centre of the trader window. Only when the money plate is as wide as the window (Dark UI); the vanilla window stays as it is."
msgstr "The trader's money at the centre of the trader window. Only when the money plate is as wide as the window (Dark UI); the vanilla window stays as it is."

msgid "Random"
msgstr "Random"

msgid "Character editor"
msgstr "Character editor"

msgid "Random name button"
msgstr "Random name button"

msgid "A button next to the name in the character editor (new game, recruiting, surgery): a random name from the game's name lists, female or male by the character. A mod that replaces the lists is used too."
msgstr "A button next to the name in the character editor (new game, recruiting, surgery): a random name from the game's name lists, female or male by the character. A mod that replaces the lists is used too."

msgid "Performance"
msgstr "Performance"

msgid "Skip moves to the same place"
msgstr "Skip moves to the same place"

msgid "The game moves the names above characters every frame, mostly to the same place, and the interface redraws all of them each time. Such moves are skipped - more frames with the interface shown."
msgstr "The game moves the names above characters every frame, mostly to the same place, and the interface redraws all of them each time. Such moves are skipped - more frames with the interface shown."

msgid "Skip unchanged UI geometry"
msgstr "Skip unchanged UI geometry"

msgid "Skip unchanged name positions and repeated relative sizes of plain interface widgets. Real pixel size changes, derived controls and explicit refreshes still work."
msgstr "Skip unchanged name positions and repeated relative sizes of plain interface widgets. Real pixel size changes, derived controls and explicit refreshes still work."
